  {
    "id": "4deaa96c-3a3e-5e3b-abfc-38081d277800",
    "pack": "myth-speakers",
    "kind": "feat",
    "slug": "feat:fools-fleeting-plan",
    "name": "Fool's Fleeting Plan",
    "level": 6,
    "rarity": "rare",
    "traits": ["mythic"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "myth-speakers"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "When Aercelys, hero-god of fools and fire, dove into the funeral pyre of his beloved daughter, he seemed a fool without thought for his safety. Yet when he returned with her body, he showed the slow rise of her chest, and those who doubted became the fools."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "You carry Aercelys's spark within you, which protects you from rash decisions. You do not trigger reactions when you use an action that you gained from being "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "6517bbf2-8085-534b-be6a-187d52739fa0"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.cKvGJCD8VdHOU0rq"
    },
    "data": {
      "category": "class"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "253aba09-4cd2-530b-bcfb-aa21fab014f2",
    "pack": "myth-speakers",
    "kind": "feat",
    "slug": "feat:forward-gaze-into-life",
    "name": "Forward Gaze Into Life",
    "level": 8,
    "rarity": "uncommon",
    "traits": ["concentrate", "divine", "exemplar", "vitality", "void"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "myth-speakers"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Frequency",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " once per hour"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Despite the constant cold of death at your back, you keep your gaze forward into the realm of life. You release two "
          },
          {
            "type": "template",
            "shape": "cone",
            "size": 15
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", aimed exactly opposite each other, one ahead of you that deals "
          },
          {
            "type": "damage",
            "instances": [
              {
                "formula": "5d10",
                "damageType": "vitality"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " damage and one behind you that deals "
          },
          {
            "type": "damage",
            "instances": [
              {
                "formula": "5d10",
                "damageType": "void"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " damage, each with a "
          },
          {
            "type": "check",
            "statistic": "save:reflex",
            "dc": {
              "against": "class-dc"
            },
            "basic": true
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " save against your class DC. Creatures that critically fail also take 5 persistent damage, of the same damage type dealt ("
          },
          {
            "type": "damage",
            "instances": [
              {
                "formula": "5",
                "damageType": "vitality",
                "category": "persistent"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " or "
          },
          {
            "type": "damage",
            "instances": [
              {
                "formula": "5",
                "damageType": "void",
                "category": "persistent"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ")."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.ix1fhe9ttnvFLgmi"
    },
    "data": {
      "category": "class",
      "prerequisites": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "trespasser in death's realm"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "action": {
        "cost": "two",
        "frequency": {
          "max": 1,
          "per": "hour"
        }
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "94a19979-1c68-5f43-93fc-2b26b7c736a8",
    "pack": "myth-speakers",
    "kind": "feat",
    "slug": "feat:griefs-fury",
    "name": "Grief's Fury",
    "level": 10,
    "rarity": "rare",
    "traits": ["archetype", "concentrate", "emotion", "mental"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "myth-speakers"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Frequency",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " once per day"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Trigger",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Your bonded partner gains the dying condition or their dying value would increase."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "A lost love. A broken spear. Rage burning through a hero-god. When a myth speaks of a wounded partner, the hero-god often rejects the future. Too many find themselves on a battlefield, clutching a body that they swore to protect. In that moment, the wellspring of power ignites."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Increase the value of your "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "cd164d22-2d8e-5fd2-b8b2-03e1360df1e7"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " condition by 1, to a maximum of "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "cd164d22-2d8e-5fd2-b8b2-03e1360df1e7",
            "label": "Doomed 3"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". You gain a +2 status bonus to attack rolls against any creature that attacked or dealt damage to your partner in the last minute. If you reduce a creature to 0 HP that attacked or damaged your partner, you gain temporary Hit Points equal to twice their level. These benefits last until your bonded partner is no longer "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "e1a78dad-4887-518e-9120-e58b7009ebfd"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " or for 1 minute, whichever duration is shorter."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.S6X3zFOCLVgRY2gd"
    },
    "data": {
      "category": "class",
      "prerequisites": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Hero-God's Bond"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "action": {
        "cost": "reaction",
        "trigger": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Your bonded partner gains the dying condition or their dying value would increase."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "frequency": {
          "max": 1,
          "per": "day"
        },
        "selfEffect": "c203339f-8bc4-59f7-9d50-bedae3f9ea02"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "448cf0f9-ed52-5e2b-b5cc-6a4513e5cd09",
    "pack": "myth-speakers",
    "kind": "feat",
    "slug": "feat:hero-gods-bond",
    "name": "Hero-God's Bond",
    "level": 6,
    "rarity": "rare",
    "traits": ["archetype"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "myth-speakers"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "At times, the myth of a hero-god includes a favored partner or a bonded ally, such as the hero-gods of promises and shield-bearers, Upion and Warrick. When you gain this feat, select an ally. They are your bonded partner. While you and your bonded partner are on the same plane, you and your bonded partner always have the same doomed value (defaulting to the highest value), so when your bonded partner's doomed condition would increase or be set to a specific amount, your doomed value also increases to match (if it is lower than your current doomed value). When either of you are "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "c0cd649a-7029-5174-a5b4-678f51598dec"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", the other knows this immediately, as well as the distance and direction to the dying partner's location. When either of you attempts a recovery check, as long as the other is on the same plane, you gain a +2 circumstance bonus to the check. You can communicate telepathically with your bonded partner as long as you are within 60 feet of each other."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "You can change your bonded partner by spending 1 week of downtime bonding with another ally."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.j9TEwIPFOUTZfVn3"
    },
    "data": {
      "category": "class",
      "prerequisites": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Warrior of Legend Dedication"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "f9e42ecb-faf9-5607-b7db-4dd52465c055",
    "pack": "myth-speakers",
    "kind": "feat",
    "slug": "feat:heroic-weakness",
    "name": "Heroic Weakness",
    "level": 14,
    "rarity": "rare",
    "traits": ["mythic"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "myth-speakers"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "As word of your faith spreads, so too does word of your foibles and weaknesses. Where originally these disadvantages may have been myths themselves, or simply manifestations of ill fortune or chance, when you take this feat, one of those weaknesses becomes real."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Work with your GM to choose your heroic weakness—it must be to a specific damage type and must be associated with a specific condition, both of which must be elements that are going to be significant parts of your story's future. For example, you could choose for a weakness to be spirit damage caused to you by a follower of a rival god, physical damage from a specific category of weapon, void damage caused by a specific kind of undead, or fire damage taken in a certain part of the world or from creatures from that part of the world. The amount of weakness you gain to this damage is equal to twice your level."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "But with this new weakness comes a new source of power, for when your foes would take advantage of your weakness, you can use the pain and humiliation to bolster your own resolve. You gain the "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "26151845-7145-5379-b2dc-93985324e6c2"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " reaction."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "key": "GrantItem",
        "item": "26151845-7145-5379-b2dc-93985324e6c2"
      }
    ],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.4iEQ5zQSTRls3Kln"
    },
    "data": {
      "category": "class",
      "prerequisites": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Godling Dedication; hero-god accomplishment"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "prerequisiteClauses": [
        {
          "text": "Godling Dedication",
          "predicate": ["feat:godling-dedication"]
        },
        {
          "text": "hero-god accomplishment"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "f2ca29c1-58b9-5394-abfd-8f406c19798d",
    "pack": "myth-speakers",
    "kind": "feat",
    "slug": "feat:hydras-bond",
    "name": "Hydra's Bond",
    "level": 4,
    "rarity": "rare",
    "traits": ["mythic"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "myth-speakers"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "When the hero-gods built Pol-Sylirica and its seven armies, they feared betrayal from within. They took inspiration from the multi-headed hydra, and bound the seven armies together with supernatural ties to make them behave as if they shared one body. Following these tactics, during daily preparations, you can select a number of willing creatures equal to half your level to be part of your hydra's bond. Members of the same hydra's bond always know if another member is telling the truth."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "When a member of the hydra's bond saves against an effect that would have them act against their allies (such as the "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "6f53a234-670f-5b02-a986-7cce57585fc8"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " condition, a "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "54bcf730-ab6d-5ba7-9747-86a6debbd00c"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " spell, or other mental effects that would give an ally the "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "3f5dc8b4-dcc0-5a99-8501-aff382e8d341"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " condition), you can spend a Mythic Point to allow that character to attempt the save at mythic proficiency. If a member of the hydra's bond fails a save against such an effect, other members automatically know that the target is controlled or under the influence of a mental effect. In addition, all members of the hydra's bond gain a +2 circumstance bonus to any roll made to counteract that effect."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.HnXZCpqRaj1nInjh"
    },
    "data": {
      "category": "class"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "ffe15fdf-393c-54f3-98d8-c35b71731444",
    "pack": "myth-speakers",
    "kind": "feat",
    "slug": "feat:martyrs-parry",
    "name": "Martyr's Parry",
    "level": 8,
    "rarity": "rare",
    "traits": ["archetype"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "myth-speakers"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Trigger",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " A creature attacks your bonded partner."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Requirements",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " You are wielding a weapon that has the parry trait, and your bonded partner is within reach of one of your melee Strikes with that weapon."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "You intercede to absorb the triggering attack. Your bonded partner gains a +2 circumstance bonus to their AC. If the attack still hits, you take the triggering attack's damage instead of your bonded partner, though the attack still uses your bonded partner's defenses for the purposes of determining if it hit or critically hit."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "355246fb-6be1-52c1-bd32-33fe703f5748"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.Item.fGwd5g6yHzcyeCG1"
    },
    "data": {
      "category": "class",
      "prerequisites": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Hero-God's Bond"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "action": {
        "cost": "reaction",
        "requirementsText": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "You are wielding a weapon that has the parry trait, and your bonded partner is within reach of one of your melee Strikes with that weapon."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "trigger": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "A creature attacks your bonded partner."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
